<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quĕrĭbundus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		queror, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>complaining</i> (rare but class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totos lustrat queribunda penates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 7, 126</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magnā et queribundā voce
					dicebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sull. 10, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 583</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
